[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/comments/398252342","html_url":"https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/issues/8009#issuecomment-398252342","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bokeh/bokeh/issues/8009","id":398252342,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5ODI1MjM0Mg==","user":{"login":"MikeWoodward","id":17951720,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTUxNzIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17951720?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeWoodward","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeWoodward","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeWoodward/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeWoodward/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeWoodward/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeWoodward/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeWoodward/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeWoodward/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeWoodward/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeWoodward/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeWoodward/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-06-19T02:13:38Z","updated_at":"2018-06-19T02:26:34Z","body":"There's another related issue I've been unable to duplicate in self-contained code. When updating the min_date, max_date, and value attributes via a callback, the date is sometimes shifted by two days for recent days (in the last year). If you change these attributes to dates in the 1960's, the offset can be two years or more.\r\n\r\nI'm trying to create a smaller example, but here's the line of code that updates one of the attributes:\r\n```\r\n            self.panel.child.children[1].children[0].children[0].value = \\\r\n                min_date\r\n```\r\nwhen min_date is 1969-12-31, the value actually displayed is Wed Apr 05 1967\r\n